--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

The licence above covers gscore itself. Some of what gscore carries is
somebody else's work and keeps its own licence, which the MIT licence above
does not and cannot change.

Bravura
    internal/smufl/data/Bravura.otf, embedded in the binary.
    Copyright © Steinberg Media Technologies GmbH, with Reserved Font Name
    "Bravura". Licensed under the SIL Open Font License, Version 1.1 — the
    full text is in internal/smufl/data/LICENSE.txt.

    The OFL allows the font to be bundled and redistributed with software,
    which is what gscore does. It does not allow the font to be sold on its
    own, and it keeps the reserved name.

    internal/smufl/data/bravura-bboxes.json is from the same place and
    under the same licence: it is the glyphBBoxes object of Bravura's own
    redist/Bravura.json, which is the font's SMuFL metadata — Bravura's
    account of where the ink is in each of its glyphs. Only that object is
    kept, and the keys are sorted, so the file is a subset of the upstream
    one rather than a rewriting of it. It carries the font name and version
    it was taken from, and a test checks those still match the font that is
    shipped beside it.

PKWARE DCL decompression
    internal/pkware. Finale's older .mus files compress their music with
    the PKWARE Data Compression Library format, which nothing in Go's
    standard library reads. The knowledge of that format in internal/pkware
    — the three tables of code lengths, the inverted canonical code
    assignment, and the length and distance encodings — is Mark Adler's,
    taken from blast.c in zlib's contrib/blast.

    That file is under the zlib licence, reproduced below, and this is an
    altered version of it, which that licence asks be said plainly: it is
    Go rather than C, it builds its whole output rather than flushing a
    sliding window, and its limits and its errors are gscore's. gscore does
    not claim to have written the original.

        Copyright (C) 2003, 2012, 2013 Mark Adler

        This software is provided 'as-is', without any express or implied
        warranty.  In no event will the author be held liable for any damages
        arising from the use of this software.

        Permission is granted to anyone to use this software for any purpose,
        including commercial applications, and to alter it and redistribute it
        freely, subject to the following restrictions:

        1. The origin of this software must not be misrepresented; you must not
           claim that you wrote the original software. If you use this software
           in a product, an acknowledgment in the product documentation would be
           appreciated but is not required.
        2. Altered source versions must be plainly marked as such, and must not be
           misrepresented as being the original software.
        3. This notice may not be removed or altered from any source distribution.

        Mark Adler    madler@alumni.caltech.edu

The .mus format itself
    internal/format/enigma/mus*.go. Finale's older format was never published
    beyond one preliminary note from 1996, and what gscore knows of it was
    worked out from files by the finale-file-parser project, which is MIT
    licensed. No code was copied from it: what was taken is facts about a
    file format, which are nobody's property. docs/finale-mus.md says which
    facts, and credits it.

SMuFL glyph names
    internal/smufl/data/glyphnames.json, the standard mapping of musical
    glyph names to codepoints, from the Standard Music Font Layout
    specification.

Soundfonts
    No soundfont is in this repository. The macOS and Windows packages fetch
    GeneralUser GS at build time and ship it inside the package; it is by
    S. Christian Collins and is free to use for any purpose, including
    commercially, under its own terms. Anything else a user downloads
    through gscore is likewise under its own terms and not under this
    licence.

MusicXML test suite
    internal/format/musicxml/testdata/suite, 182 files used by the tests and
    by nothing that ships. Copyright © 2016-2026 Michael Scott Asato
    Cuthbert, MIT licensed; the licence is in that directory. Written
    originally by Reinhold Kainhofer for LilyPond and now kept by the W3C
    Music Notation Community Group.

Go dependencies
    github.com/sinshu/go-meltysynth — MIT
    github.com/webview/webview_go — MIT
    github.com/yuin/goldmark — MIT (builds the documentation pages of the
    web site; not part of the program)
